{
"opening": "This release focuses on stabilizing the command-line interface and introducing new validation capabilities for version strings. We are addressing critical bugs in argument handling and adding a robust method to verify version format compliance.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m07",
"text": "Calling the pysemver script without arguments must raise a SystemExit error instead of crashing with an AttributeError. Invoking 'pysemver bump' without arguments should print the subcommand's help text and exit gracefully."
},
{
"id": "m12",
"text": "The internal regex used for parsing semantic versions must be updated to match the official specification from semver.org. This ensures that invalid or non-compliant version strings are correctly rejected during parsing operations."
},
{
"id": "m17",
"text": "The VersionInfo class must provide a static isvalid method that accepts a version string and returns a boolean indicating whether it conforms to the semantic versioning standard. The pysemver CLI must include a 'check' subcommand that utilizes this validation logic."
},
{
"id": "m19",
"text": "The CLI argument parser must use a 'func' keyword to dispatch specific subcommand handlers, replacing the previous 'which' attribute approach. Each subcommand handler should be isolated in its own function to ensure clear separation of concerns and easier extensibility."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure all public APIs behave as described above before merging these changes into the main branch."
}
